. * LOAD AND MERGE DATA * General Logic: Stata just sees rows and variables, if
>  we 
. * are matching pid and syear 1:1, then we are matching a panel to another pan
> el. 
. * If we are matching pid without syear m:1, we are matching variables for a p
> erson 
. * in a dataset that is cross-sectional to ALL years of that person in the pan
> el
. 
.         use "$IN/ppathl.dta", clear // use ppathl as a starting dataset
(SOEP-Core, v37 (EU Edition), doi:10.5684/soep.core.v37eu)

.         // This dataset contains matching information, e.g., between partners
>  in 
.         // relationships (respondent’s pid and the unique partner’s pid) or b
> etween 
.         // samples of SOEP in which the respondent was interviewed (26 differ
> ent samples)
.         keep cid pid hid syear parid partner sex gebjahr sampreg pop todjahr 
> immiyear ///
>         germborn corigin migback miginfo sexor birthregion birthregion_ew are
> fback phrf /// 
>         phrf0 phrf1 piyear

. 
.         // Merge the ‘pgen’ dataset: consolidated person-level variables from
>  
.         // various sources, providing user-friendly individual metrics
.         merge 1:1 pid syear using "$IN/pgen.dta", nogen keep(master matches)
(variable syear was long, now double to accommodate using data's values)

